<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11943" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπερί-σπαστος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not diawn hither and
				thither, not distracted</i> or <i>hindered,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				2.67.7
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕπνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philum.
				</span></i>
			 ap.<i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				45.29.57
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεωρία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Abst.</u>
					1.36
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀ.</span>”
				<i>freedom from distractions,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.521c
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Si.</u>
				41.1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παρέχεσθαί τινα ἀ.</span>
			<i>guarantee against annoyance</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BGU</u>
				1057.22
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τῆς σῆς
				εὐεργεσίας</span>
			<i>not able to be roused by</i> it, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Wi.</u>
				16.11
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					2.20.10
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>1 Ep.Cor.</u>
				7.35
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθῆσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>Epict.</u>
					1.29.59
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>uninterrupted, free from digressions,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				<u>Th.</u>
				9
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀ. τῆς ἐξουσίας</span>
			<i>the fact of</i> power <i>not passing from hand to hand,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Arist.</u>
				5
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>
			<i>continually,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαινεῖ τὸν οἶνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.
					1.1c
				</span></i>
			c.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
